    "original": "<p><i><b>A ball of mass 0.2 kg moves to the left on a </b></i><i><b>smooth horizontal surface and hits an object. </b></i><i><b>The ball moves at 1.5 m s</b></i><i><b><sup>−1</sup></b></i><i><b> towards the right </b></i><i><b>after the impact. The net force </b></i><i><b>F</b></i><i><b><sub>net</sub></b></i><i><b> acting on it </b></i><i><b>points to the right during the impact and varies </b></i><i><b>with time </b></i><i><b>t</b></i><i><b> as shown (Fig v). The area under the </b></i><i><b>graph is 0.7 N s.</b></i></p><p class=\"study-figure\"><img src=\"assets/textbook-exercises/media/f086a16ee115e5082528812e.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width:168.7px\"/></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>Fig v</b></i><i><b>t</b></i><i><b> </b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(a) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>State the physical meaning of the area under </b></i><i><b>the graph. </b></i><i><b>(1 mark)</b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(b) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>Estimate the velocity of the ball before the </b></i><i><b>collision. </b></i><i><b>(2 marks)</b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(c) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>If the average net force acting on the ball </b></i><i><b>during the impact is 17.5 N, estimate the </b></i><i><b>impact time. </b></i><i><b>(2 marks)</b></i></p>",
    "replacement": "<p><i><b>A ball of mass 0.2 kg moves to the left on a </b></i><i><b>smooth horizontal surface and hits an object. </b></i><i><b>The ball moves at 1.5 m s</b></i><i><b><sup>−1</sup></b></i><i><b> towards the right </b></i><i><b>after the impact. The net force </b></i><i><b>F</b></i><i><b><sub>net</sub></b></i><i><b> acting on it </b></i><i><b>points to the right during the impact and varies </b></i><i><b>with time </b></i><i><b>t</b></i><i><b> as shown (Fig v). The area under the </b></i><i><b>graph is 0.7 N s.</b></i></p><p class=\"study-figure\"><img src=\"assets/textbook-exercises/media/207-26-complete-labels.png\" alt=\"Net force versus time t with area 0.7 N s\" style=\"width:300px\"></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(a) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>State the physical meaning of the area under </b></i><i><b>the graph. </b></i><i><b>(1 mark)</b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(b) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>Estimate the velocity of the ball before the </b></i><i><b>collision. </b></i><i><b>(2 marks)</b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(c) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>If the average net force acting on the ball </b></i><i><b>during the impact is 17.5 N, estimate the </b></i><i><b>impact time. </b></i><i><b>(2 marks)</b></i></p>",
