  {
    "language": "eng",
    "id": "tb-208-5",
    "field": "question",
    "original": "<p><i><b>Two objects, </b></i><i><b>P</b></i><i><b> and </b></i><i><b>Q</b></i><i><b>, are projected from the same </b></i><i><b>level at the same time. </b></i><i><b>P</b></i><i><b> is projected vertically </b></i><i><b>upwards at a speed of 30 m s</b></i><i><b><sup>−1</sup></b></i><i><b> while </b></i><i><b>Q</b></i><i><b> is </b></i><i><b>projected at an angle of 60° to the vertical at a </b></i><i><b>speed of 60 m s</b></i><i><b><sup>−1</sup></b></i><i><b> (Fig d). The objects land on </b></i><i><b>positions at the same level.</b></i></p><p class=\"study-figure\"><img src=\"assets/textbook-exercises/media/bafc5228eba235f1d7a454da.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width:205.3px\"/></p><p><i><b>  </b></i><i><b>Fig d</b></i><i><b>P</b></i><i><b>Q</b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>Which of the following statements are correct?</b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(1) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>P</b></i><i><b> and </b></i><i><b>Q</b></i><i><b> land at the same time.</b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(2) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>P</b></i><i><b> and </b></i><i><b>Q</b></i><i><b> have the same acceleration </b></i><i><b>throughout their flights.</b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(3) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>P</b></i><i><b> and </b></i><i><b>Q</b></i><i><b> are momentarily at rest when they </b></i><i><b>reach their maximum height.</b></i></p><p><i><b>A </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(1) and (2) only </b></i></p><p><i><b>B </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(1) and (3) only</b></i></p><p><i><b>C </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(2) and (3) only </b></i></p><p><i><b>D </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(1), (2) and (3)</b></i></p>",
    "replacement": "<p><i><b>Two objects, </b></i><i><b>P</b></i><i><b> and </b></i><i><b>Q</b></i><i><b>, are projected from the same </b></i><i><b>level at the same time. </b></i><i><b>P</b></i><i><b> is projected vertically </b></i><i><b>upwards at a speed of 30 m s</b></i><i><b><sup>−1</sup></b></i><i><b> while </b></i><i><b>Q</b></i><i><b> is </b></i><i><b>projected at an angle of 60° to the vertical at a </b></i><i><b>speed of 60 m s</b></i><i><b><sup>−1</sup></b></i><i><b> (Fig d). The objects land on </b></i><i><b>positions at the same level.</b></i></p><p class=\"study-figure\"><img src=\"assets/textbook-exercises/media/208-5-complete-labels.png\" alt=\"Projectiles P and Q with their launch velocities and angle\" style=\"width:366px\"></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>Which of the following statements are correct?</b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(1) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>P</b></i><i><b> and </b></i><i><b>Q</b></i><i><b> land at the same time.</b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(2) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>P</b></i><i><b> and </b></i><i><b>Q</b></i><i><b> have the same acceleration </b></i><i><b>throughout their flights.</b></i></p><p><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(3) </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>P</b></i><i><b> and </b></i><i><b>Q</b></i><i><b> are momentarily at rest when they </b></i><i><b>reach their maximum height.</b></i></p><p><i><b>A </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(1) and (2) only </b></i></p><p><i><b>B </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(1) and (3) only</b></i></p><p><i><b>C </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(2) and (3) only </b></i></p><p><i><b>D </b></i><i><b> </b></i><i><b>(1), (2) and (3)</b></i></p>",
